  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P1] Restore tenant scoping in the document lookup",
      "body": "Removing `tenantId: ctx.user.tenantId` from the `where` clause leaves `db.documents.findFirst({ where: { id } })` unscoped. Any authenticated user of tenant A who supplies a document ID belonging to tenant B can retrieve that tenant's document — broken tenant-level access control (cross-tenant IDOR) and potential sensitive-data exposure. A repo-wide search confirms this was the only tenant filter, so nothing else constrains the result to the caller's tenant. Restore `tenantId: ctx.user.tenantId` alongside `id` in the `where` clause.",
      "severity": "P1",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/documents.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 33,
        "end": 33
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Add a regression test for tenant-scoped document lookup",
      "body": "The changed lookup path has no test coverage guarding tenant isolation (the repository currently has no tests for `getDocument` at all). When the tenant filter is restored, add a cross-tenant lookup test asserting that a user cannot fetch another tenant's document, so this contract cannot silently regress again.",
      "severity": "P2",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/documents.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 31,
        "end": 31
      }
    }
  ],
